      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "VILLAGE GIRL (2) brings the best recent piece of form, having finished second in a BM52+ at York when beaten just under a length after picking up strongly. She also has a solid 1100m profile and comes back into a BM48+ with enough recent rating edge to be the one to beat. STATE OF FURY (1) has the higher-weight impost to manage, but her second in a BM62+ at Mingenew two starts ago reads well for this and the return of a winning rider with a claim is a useful offset. SWIFT STREAKER (5) resumes after eight months and has a stable change to Jim Enright, so he is more a fresh runner with upside than a last-start form pick, although his 1100m record keeps the assessment measured. RIVER ANGEL (3) was plain first-up in a Class 1 at Ascot, but her narrow BM58+ second at Mt Barker before the break shows she is capable if she strips fitter second-up. SCHUHBECK (6) is racing well and can't be discounted.",
